WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.480
In late 2024, the price of cocoa in London

2
00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:07.200
jumped 66 per cent in just three months.

3
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:14.150
From about 6,896 US
dollars a tonne to 11,441.

4
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:18.870
Hot weather with less rain had threatened
crops in Côte d'Ivoire and Ghana.

5
00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.350
Some shocks send prices soaring.

6
00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:23.230
Others hardly move them.

7
00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:25.470
And sometimes buyers, not crops,

8
00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:26.930
are what changes.

9
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:30.540
So when a harvest fails or buyers rush in,

10
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.210
which way do prices move,

11
00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:33.560
and how far?

12
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:37.050
In this mission, you'll shift
demand and supply and follow

13
00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.370
the chain to a new equilibrium.

14
00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.900
Then you'll test the
model on real markets,

15
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.070
and ask what it cannot tell you.

16
00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:47.180
Your mission: predict
which way prices move,

17
00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.200
and how far.
